{"tool_name":"calcen","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"calcen","home":"http://github.com/momeara/CalCEN","summary":"CalCEN is a comprehensive and unbiased coexpression network for C. albicans.","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:42:00Z","last_update_date":"2021-04-21T11:07:32Z","tool_type":["Script","Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:calcen","credit":[{"email":"maom@umich.edu","name":"Matthew J. O\u2019Meara","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3128-5331","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"tromeara@umich.edu","name":"Teresa R. O\u2019Meara","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8901-0154","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Coding region prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0436"},{"term":"Expression correlation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3463"},{"term":"Gene functional annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3672"},{"term":"Homology-based gene prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3663"},{"term":"Network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3925"}]}],"name":"CalCEN","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1128/MSPHERE.01245-20","metadata":{"abstract":"Copyright \u00a9 2021 O\u2019Meara and O\u2019Meara. This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license.Functional characterization of open reading frames in nonmodel organisms, such as the common opportunistic fungal pathogen Candida albicans, can be labor-intensive. To meet this challenge, we built a comprehensive and unbiased coexpression network for C. albicans, which we call CalCEN, from data collected from 853 RNA sequencing runs from 18 large-scale studies deposited in the NCBI Sequence Read Archive. Retrospectively, CalCEN is highly predictive of known gene function annotations and can be synergistically combined with sequence similarity and interaction networks in Saccharomyces cerevisiae through orthology for additional accuracy in gene function prediction. To prospectively demonstrate the utility of the coexpression network in C. albicans, we predicted the function of underannotated open reading frames (ORFs) and identified CCJ1 as a novel cell cycle regulator in C. albicans. This study provides a tool for future systems biology analyses of gene function in C. albicans. We provide a computational pipeline for building and analyzing the coexpression network and CalCEN itself at http://github.com/momeara/CalCEN.","authors":[{"name":"O'Meara M.J."},{"name":"O'Meara T.R."}],"date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"mSphere","title":"DeORFanizing Candida albicans Genes using Coexpression"},"pmcid":"PMC7845621","pmid":"33472984"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3053"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"CalCEN","home":"https://bio.tools/calcen","summary":"CalCEN is a comprehensive and unbiased coexpression network for C. albicans.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:calcen/script/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":18,"citations":[{"count":3,"year":"2023"},{"count":5,"year":"2021"},{"count":5,"year":"2024"},{"count":5,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1128/mSphere.01245-20","pmcid":"PMC7845621","pmid":"33472984","ref_count":55,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"}